305 #edb/ref 1071 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394305 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a27a3c1e-ad3c-56e4-aa1a-d2aedbc7058d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394305 #edb/ref 1074 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (-9)}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394306 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5d1bd593-f01f-5378-b1fe-6d41f9f01e52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394307 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394307 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394307 #edb/ref